Discovered while fixing ttrb-fsx9.

API_BASE in app/javascript/lib/api.ts is the relative '/api/v1'. happy-dom resolves relative URLs against http://localhost:3000, so any vitest test that renders a component firing an unmocked fetch reaches for a real server. ttrb-fsx9 fixed the two files that did this today (EntryContent, SettingsDialog), but nothing stops the next one.

Proposal: override global.fetch in test/setup.ts so an unmocked call never leaves the process.

Verified during ttrb-fsx9: adding

  global.fetch = ((input: RequestInfo | URL) => {
    const url = typeof input === 'string' ? input : String(input);
    throw new Error(`Unmocked fetch to ${url}. Mock @/lib/api (or global.fetch) in this test.`);
  }) as typeof fetch;

keeps the full suite green (27 files / 522 tests) and does stop the real request: reverting EntryContent.test.tsx to its pre-fix state with the guard in place produced 27 passing tests and zero ECONNREFUSED output.

Caveat that needs deciding before merging it: the guard is silent, not loud. request() in api.ts is async, so a synchronous throw becomes a rejected promise that component-level .catch handlers swallow. The result is that unmocked boundaries stop being visible at all, trading today's ECONNREFUSED noise for silence. Worth pairing the throw with a console.error naming the URL so the output still flags it, or finding a way to fail the test outright.

Not done under ttrb-fsx9 because test/setup.ts is outside that issue's stated scope (two named test files).
